github.com/belluikit/goffmpeg-libs/android_arm
==============================================

FFmpeg (https://ffmpeg.org) built for android_arm as shared libraries, so that an app
ships them and a user can replace them (LGPL 2.1 section 6b), in two codec
sets (belluikit/goffmpeg#41). An app's binary loads one of them.

shared/ holds the media set: MP3, WAV, MP4, WebM, Ogg and HLS, with H.264,
VP9 and AV1 video and AAC and Opus audio.

  libavcodec-goffmpeg.so libavformat-goffmpeg.so libavutil-goffmpeg.so libswresample-goffmpeg.so libswscale-goffmpeg.so

shared-audio/ holds the audio set: MP3, WAV and Opus (in Ogg), with no
libswscale and no libavdevice.

  libavcodec-goffmpeg-audio.so libavformat-goffmpeg-audio.so libavutil-goffmpeg-audio.so libswresample-goffmpeg-audio.so

FFmpeg version: N-125841-ge2bc6d88cd (git revision e2bc6d88cd68184288c16570e04881c3a426a05a).
Local patch: shared/'s libavcodec is built with one change to FFmpeg,
goffmpeg's patches/0001-mediacodecdec-stall-before-first-frame.patch
(belluikit/goffmpeg#88, 2026-11-13). It modifies libavcodec/mediacodecdec.c:
a MediaCodec that takes no input and returns no frame for 2 s before its
first frame now ends with an error, which goffmpeg turns into software
decoding, instead of a decode that never returns. shared-audio/ has no
MediaCodec decoder and is unchanged, as are the other libraries in shared/.

